<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- ======================================================================
     THE PLANS ARE NOT WRITTEN HERE, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.

     What a product sells, in which currency and at what price, is the
     PRODUCT's answer and not the cockpit's (rail R11). So this file carries no
     records at all: it calls the seeder, which reads whatever the product
     registered and puts it in the table. On a machine where no product has
     registered anything the table stays empty and the screen says so honestly.

     WHY noupdate IS ABSENT (i.e. 0). The call must run on every upgrade, not
     only on the first install: the product's overlay may be installed after
     this module, or gain a plan later, and a seeding that ran once would leave
     the new one missing until somebody noticed. The seeder itself never
     touches a plan that already exists, so a re-run cannot undo a price
     somebody has corrected.

     ⚠ THE METHOD IT CALLS CARRIES `@api.model`, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING
     (ledger F45): a `function` with no arguments reads the FIRST argument as
     the records to call the method on, and without the marker the upgrade dies
     on "not enough values to unpack" naming THIS LINE rather than the method.

     ⚠ AND A BANDED PLAN IS CREATED WITH ITS BANDS IN ONE WRITE (ledger F60).
     The model refuses a banded plan with no bands, correctly — so a data file
     that made the plan and then added the bands would fail in between and take
     the whole upgrade with it. That is the second reason the seeding is a
     method and not a set of records here.
     ====================================================================== -->
<odoo>

    <function model="biz.plan" name="ensure_seeded"/>

</odoo>
